<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel"> 
      <p xml:id="Aink191-kilavi">
       varaiyātu vantoḻukun talaimakaṉ talaimakaṭku vaḷaikoṇṭu vantu koṭuttuḻi, paṇṭaivaḷai pōlāvāy melintuḻi nīṅkā nalaṉuṭaiyavō ivai eṉat talaimakaḷ melivucollit tōḻi varaivukaṭāyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
       The confidante suggesting marriage, talking about the frailty of the heroine, saying 'Are these good ones that do not leave [her wrists] when [she] is frail [= loses weight], unlike the previous bangles [she had]?' when the hero, having brought [new] bangles, gave [them], still coming without [intentions] to marry.</p>
  </div> 
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink193">
<l>valampuri yuḻuta vārmaṇa laṭaikarai</l>
<l>yilaṅkukatir mutta miruḷkeṭa vimaikkun</l>
<l>tuṟaikeḻu koṇkanī tanta</l>
<l>vaṟaipuṉal vālvaḷai nallavō tāmē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>Oh man from the sea that has ghats</l>
        <l>In which pearls that shine with rays sparkle</l>
        <l>So that darkness gets lost,</l>
        <l>In the shore where overflowing sand which is furrowed by right-spiralled conches settles!</l>
        <l>The pure bangles [from] the beating floods that you gave [her] —</l>
        <l>They are good ones, right?</l>      </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
